# --- setuptools build output ---------------------------------------------
# `uv build` writes here. KEPT after the PyInstaller path was deleted on 2026-09-27:
# un-ignoring them means the next `git add -A` sweeps in a wheel and a second copy of desk/.
# `*.spec` stays for the same reason -- PyInstaller prefers a stale spec once one exists.
build/
dist/
*.spec

# --- python -------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# --- not kept in the repo, by decision 2026-09-05 -----------------------
# The pre-SQLite YAML ledger and the one-time migration that read it. Backed
# up outside the repo; the book in book/hub.db is authoritative going forward.
# The author: "we dont need the old archive going forward."
archive/

# Claude-generated design specs and process docs. The author: "we dont need that
# superpower docs or anything claude generated design spec docs."
docs/

# Reviewer and agent scratch. `.probe/` is here because two subagent diagnostic
# scripts were actually committed on 2026-09-07 (d6df16e): an audit workflow ran 45
# agents with filesystem access, they wrote probes into .probe/ and scratch/, and a
# blanket `git add -A` swept in the one that was not already ignored. scratch/ was
# ignored and survived; .probe/ was not. The lesson is the pattern, not the two
# files: anything a helper process writes belongs to a name git already refuses.
tmpwork/
scratch/
.probe/
# shots.py renders the REAL book -- every tab, with the real profile name -- as SVG, which is
# greppable plaintext. It was not ignored, so one run plus `git add -A` would have committed a
# picture of the positions into a repo that is about to be published.
shots/
.trash/
probe*.db

# --- THE DATA ------------------------------------------------------------
# The author, 2026-09-07: "data is data and code is code. ideally i think it's better to
# have the data and code separated. so this repo is pure tool instead of tool
# combined with data."
#
# The book is the owner's positions and balances. It was tracked until 2026-09-07 and the
# history is still in git, so nothing is lost -- but going forward the repo carries
# the TOOL and the SCHEMA (book/schema.sql), never the record. Point the tool at a
# book with $TRADING_DESK_BOOK; create one with `python3 book/migrate.py --new`.
#
# This also fixes a coupling that had already bitten: the tests read the live book
# as a fixture, so recording a real trade turned three of them red.
# BY EXTENSION, NOT BY PATH. `book/hub.db` only ignored the book at ITS path -- a book
# created anywhere else in the tree, or under any other name, was committable. Nothing here
# is a database that belongs in git: the schema is `book/schema.sql`, and every test and
# screenshot builds its own in a temp directory. The author, 2026-09-25: "just make sure we dont
# record it later on."
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# THE THESES HAD NO RULE, which is the gap that mattered most. 51 files of research notes,
# observations and chart images were tracked until 2026-09-07 and then removed -- with
# nothing stopping the next `git add -A` from putting them back. This is a tool repo; the
# claims live wherever they write them.
theses/

# Broker statements, in any form. None has ever been committed; the point is that a PDF
# dropped in the tree to be read from should not be a thing to notice afterwards.
*.pdf
statements/

# --- obsidian -----------------------------------------------------------
# Per-machine UI state, not content.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.DS_Store
